      "writtenOn": "2026-03-18T14:08:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is usually not a good (testing) pattern. Try not to rely on threads sleeping. What can be done is to pass a mock of ExecutorService to the SubmitRequirementsEvaluatorImpl constructor. The mocked ExecutorService shall return a mocked Future when executor.submit is called. The mocked \nFuture shall throw a TimeoutException when its Future.get(timeout) method is called. It shall throw that exception immediately. We do not really need to test that Future.get(timeout) really waits that long before timing out (this is guaranteed by JDK). Instead we test that the result is correct when evaluation times out.",
      "revId": "9f7ee7af1b831b8145d3a309461add618aeaecac",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
